From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:30:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 125/202] [ae-patch] Settle a Claude subagent that died before
 its first lull or across a restart

A Claude Code subagent child that never records a return was settled only by
the staleness timer armed on its first idle lull. A child that died before any
lull never got a timer, and a server restart dropped every pending timer, so
the rail showed it Running and its parent "Waiting on 1 agent" indefinitely.

The first running edge (external_session_status) now arms the same 60-minute
check, and a background sweep at server startup reads the sub-agent rows whose
persisted status is running in one query, settles idle the Claude children
quiet past the cap with no recorded completion, and re-arms the rest for the
time remaining. The settle check reads the row's live_status when the cache is
empty, which is what readers see after a restart. The sweep is best-effort: a
failure logs and never blocks startup.
